directions.mechanism:
Add a REFUSABLE government command for both player and AI, for example AssertCivilianAuthority { nation, institution, scope }. It names a concrete authority change, such as bringing senior Army appointments under the civilian ministry.

Legality:
- an electoral state with a completed, unrestricted ballot (elected && unrestricted_mandate && !awaiting_first_election);
- an established civilian record (existing `established_civilian_record`, at least 6 months under the same party);
- a specific Army institution with known live leverage above 0;
- current authoritarianism above 0.20 (the civilian-control guard, see D2);
- no unresolved dispute already open;
- a political-capital price.

Compliance, owned by the server plan: prospective acceptance = effective loyalty − W·leverage·scope. This has the same structure as the existing `army_programme_veto_loyalty` (W .45 there). The institution refuses below the existing 0.35 line.
- If it complies, live leverage falls through an army_authority update like `consolidate_transfer`. That reduction is the AI's positive objective, because it shrinks future confidence-penalty and programme-veto exposure.
- If it refuses, store a DisputeRecord in GovState: institution identity, order receipt, issuing party, scope, refusal date and status. It is serde-default empty, so an old save has no dispute.

Resolutions, quoted from the same plan:
- negotiate a narrower scope, which is re-tested;
- withdraw, which clears the dispute at a cost;
- enforce, which keeps it open.

Only an unresolved, enforced dispute accrues a separate authority pressure. It has no D >= .25 requirement and stops the moment the dispute resolves. When it fires, it reuses `break_electoral` with the existing 'removes the elected government' headline, because the event is a military removal of an elected government. It never double-charges an annulment or programme veto.

The AI decides at the existing 0.02 draw site in `stratagems::ai_stratagems` and never manufactures disputes. The government module draws no RNG.
